          "32": 262,
          "33": 273,
          "34": 286,
          "35": 290,
          "36": 295,
          "<色調 0, -30, -80, 50>\r\n<マップ名Library_Dream >": 0,
          "EV001": 1,
          "EV002": 2,
          "EV003": 3,
          "EV004": 4,
          "EV005": 5,
          "\\c[2]No matter how many sacrifices we make,\nit's all supposed to lead to the future of the world.\n\nI believed that... but how many years have we wasted?": 6,
          "\\c[2]The favor keeps tormenting people.\n\nBut it's the only thing holding the world together,\nthe only thing keeping it from falling apart.": 7,
          "\\c[2]How could a wedge, shaped by the end, ever hold the world together?\nIf fate itself has promised its demise,\nhow could one ever hope for the future?": 8,
          "\\c[2]I've never liked the word 'fate.'\nBut the more we chase the truth, the more fitting it seems.\nLife is meant to end—because that's just how it is.": 9,
          "\\c[2]I can feel Maruoris-sama's pain... It's unbearable.\nWe've done nothing but drag this world through endless suffering.\nIt's so clear now, yet we are too late to stop it.": 10,
          "\\c[2]Gwirionedd-sama.\nPlease, save the world.\nPlease... save Maruoris-sama.": 11,
          "EV006": 12,
          "EV007<SURLY>": 13,
          "\"Could it be... are you there, Messenger-san?\"": 14,
          "\"Please, I beg of you.\nGo to Maruoris-sama's side.\"": 15,
          "\"You're my only hope...\"": 16,
          "\\c[2]Rape": 17,
          "Leave": 18,
          "It seems I can't touch her body...": 19,
          "\"I've always... wanted to meet you.\nMaruoris-sama adores you...\"": 20,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #1": 22,
          "A, a, a, a, a, a,\nI, I, I, I, I, I,\nU, u, u, u, u, u,\nE, e, e, e, e, e.": 23,
          "O,  o,  o,  o,  o,  o,\nKa, ka, ka, ka, ka, ka,\nKi, ki, ki, ki, ki, ki,\nKu, ku, ku, ku, ku, ku.": 24,
          "   C     R     E     D     I     U     R\nM     A     R     U     O     R     I     S": 25,
          "Dad         laughs        a lot.\nMom           is            kind.\n             Haha.": 26,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #2": 28,
          "Starting today, I'm going to keep a diary.\nI don't know how much longer I will be able to stay with\nMaruoris-sama, the thought of separation is quite terrifying.": 29,
          "That's why I'm starting this diary today.\nEven if we end up separated...\nI want to always remember Maruoris-sama.": 30,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #3": 32,
          "Maruoris-sama was very focused on his research as usual.\nSo, I finally gathered my courage and asked:\n\"Maruoris-sama, what kind of research are you working on?\"\nAnd Maruoris-sama actually answered me.": 33,
          "\"I'm trying to find a way to save the world.\"\n\nOnce again, I was reminded of just how amazing Maruoris-sama is.": 34,
          "I can't stop thinking about this research to save the world.\nSo today, I managed to gather my courage and ask him about it.\n\n": 35,
          "But Maruoris-sama looked a little troubled and said:\n\n\"If you knew, you'd end up hating me.\"": 36,
          "\"If it's research to save the world, no matter what it is...\nI could never hate you, Maruoris-sama.\" That's what I told him.\nEven so, he still looked troubled...\nand in the end, he didn't tell me anything today.": 37,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #4": 39,
          "I'm scared.\nThere's something outside.\nI can hear the growls of a beast.": 40,
          "There is a monster of Crimson Wrath roaming around.\nMaruoris-sama is far away for his research right now.\nIf I get attacked... if I get killed... I'm sorry.\nMaruoris-sama, I've always... always... admired you.": 41,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #5": 43,
          "I want to be strong like Maruoris-sama too.\nBut... would saying that just trouble him?\n\nI'm hopeless when it comes to magic or strength.": 44,
          "Maruoris-sama is amazing.\nNo matter how huge the monster is, he takes it down in an instant.\nHe even sent one flying with just a single kick.": 45,
          "It was so ridiculous and so incredible, I couldn't help but laugh.\nThe monster didn't even twitch after that.\n\nStarting today, I think I'll practice my kicks too.": 46,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #6": 48,
          "When I ask Maruoris-sama why he's so strong,\nhe always looks just a little sad...\nand he never gives me an answer.": 49,
          "I know I must be bothering him,\nbut I just can't stop thinking about it!!\nMaruoris-sama is brilliant, his strength and magic are incredible.\nI want to be strong and smart like him too.": 50,
          "I kept asking, and eventually, he told me.\nMaruoris-sama once had a master!\nBut... he said he hates them.\nI didn't ask anything more after that.": 51,
          "A mentor that Maruoris-sama hates...\nI can't help but wonder what kind of person they were.\nWere they even stronger than Maruoris-sama?": 52,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #7": 54,
          "How does magic even work? I can't stop thinking about it.\nMaruoris-sama uses this cool, black magic.\nNo matter what kind of monster attacks him,\nhe takes them all down with it.": 55,
          "I tried practicing magic, but I don't get it at all.\nI even tried to focus something black to appear from my fingertips.\nIt just made me feel like I was playing some kind of game,\nand honestly, it was kind of embarrassing.": 56,
          "If... back then...\nIf that horde of monsters hadn't attacked...\nWould I have already outgrown silly games like this?\nWould I be back in my village, falling in love with some boy?": 57,
          "...Sometimes, I hate myself. I catch myself thinking,\n\"Why didn't Maruoris-sama come sooner?\"\nAnd I hate that I feel that way.": 58,
          "The truth is, I was supposed to die too.\nI have to live for everyone in the village who couldn't.": 59,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #8": 61,
          "Today, I asked Maruoris-sama how to use magic.\nTo my surprise, he refused!! But what shocked me even more\nwas when he said he didn't really understand it himself.": 62,
          "He told me it just started working one day...\nBut I know that's a lie. Maruoris-sama is terrible at lying.\nIt always shows in his eyes and the way he talks.": 63,
          "I want to use magic too.\nMy dream is to become like Maruoris-sama.\nSo I have to figure out how to use it, fast.": 64,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #9": 66,
          "I asked Maruoris-sama if he had a lover.\nHe just said:\n\"I've lived a life completely unrelated to such things.\"": 67,
          "I couldn't help but think... what a waste.\nBut at the same time, I think I finally understand\nthe secret behind Maruoris-sama's strength.\nHe never had time for love, he spent his whole life training.": 68,
          "Even so, I wish I could talk to him more.\nWhenever he leaves for his research,\nhe doesn't come back until the next morning.\nAnd he never takes me to his lab... It gets lonely.": 69,
          "...But more than anything,\nI'm scared of the monsters that come at night.": 70,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #10": 72,
          "Today... I followed Maruoris-sama.\n\nI just couldn't help it.\nI wanted to know what kind of research he was doing.": 73,
          "The place where he worked felt terrifying.\nI don't know why, but my whole body felt so cold.\nAnd there... I saw Maruoris-sama,\nputting that black magic into a lifeless human body.": 74,
          "I gasped without thinking.\nI'm sure he noticed me.\nI don't remember much after that,\nbut before I knew it, I was back home.": 75,
          "Maruoris-sama... is that really research to save the world?\nIt was terrifying.\nHe told me if I knew, I might hate him...\nAnd right now, I feel so scared, I think he might have been right.": 76,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #11": 78,
          "Maruoris-sama talked to me about his research...\nbut I didn't really understand.\nThat black magic... it's actually something terrible.\nHe said it's the very thing that will destroy the world.": 79,
          "\"You're using world-ending magic... to save the world?\"\nThat's what I asked. And he said, \"Yes.\"\nBut I still don't get it.\nI was too scared to ask about the dead people.": 80,
          "Maruoris-sama told me I can come see his research next time.\nHe said it's his way of making up for scaring me.\nBut if that's the case, then why not show me today?\nIs he trying to hide something?": 81,
          "I was scared... but still. I know that Maruoris-sama is kind.\nEven if it's frightening,\nI believe this research truly is meant to save the world.\nThere's no way I could ever hate him.": 82,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #12": 84,
          "There's not much left for me to study anymore.\nI want a new book.\nI wonder if there are any left behind in the ruins of the village.": 85,
          "But I'm too weak to even go outside properly.\nIt's frustrating.\nI want to grow stronger. I want to use magic.\nAnd yet, Maruoris-sama refuses to teach me anything.": 86,
          "I know I'm being selfish... but sometimes, I can't help but think—\nWhy is Maruoris-sama so... stingy?\nI just want to be strong too.\nI don't want to be stuck inside forever.": 87,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #13": 89,
          "Maruoris-sama showed me his research today.\nHe told me that if the black magic is successfully\nimplanted into a body, one can achieve immortality.\nI truly believed then, this research is meant to save the world.": 90,
          "But the motionless people around me...\nThey were all failures.\nMaruoris-sama stated it plainly:\n\"We abduct people, kill them, and await the rare success.\"": 91,
          "At that moment, Maruoris-sama felt like someone else entirely.\nThinking that these lifeless bodies once had families, just like me,\nI saw him as no different from the monsters we feared.": 92,
          "Comparing the failed corpses to the successful immortal bodies,\nhe said he was trying to uncover the conditions for success,\nwhile also investigating the true nature of this black magic.": 93,
          "I thought I was too scared to process anything at the time,\nand yet, here I am, writing it all down so clearly.": 94,
          "A terrible thought crossed my mind.\nDid Maruoris-sama save me... just to use me in this research?\nWill he eventually experiment on my body too?": 95,
          "And if he did...\nWould I even resist?\nA part of me thinks I wouldn't mind.\nA part of me wants to be useful to Maruoris-sama.": 96,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #14": 98,
          "I went back to the village that was attacked by monsters...\njust for books.\nIt was a foolish thing to do.\nIf the monsters had spotted me, I would have died.": 99,
          "But even so, I think it was worth it.\nI found plenty of books that were still intact.\nI used a basket to carry back as many as I could.\nI've outgrown picture books, so I took only books for adults.": 100,
          "I won't have to go on any more dangerous adventures for a while.\nBut staying like this forever... I can't stand the thought...!\nI even found some books that seem related to magic.\nI want to become strong enough to defeat monsters on my own.": 101,
          "And... I wasn't expecting anything, but...\nThere really wasn't anyone else alive.\nStill, I want to believe that at least one person...\nmanaged to escape.": 102,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #15": 104,
          "Maruoris-sama said:\n\"If you want more books, I'll help you find them.\nSo please... don't go wandering off alone.\"": 105,
          "And honestly, he was completely right.\nI was so caught up in wanting to do things on my own\nthat I never even considered asking him to come with me.": 106,
          "I always assumed that he was too busy with his research,\nthat he wouldn't have the time to accompany me.\nBut maybe that was just something I decided on my own.\nFrom now on, I'll rely on him more.": 107,
          "And so we went to collect the rest of the books the other day.\nI'm so happy... it's been so long since we spent time together.\nI couldn't help but stick close to him the whole time.": 108,
          "Today, Maruoris-sama wore his white mask the entire time,\nso I couldn't see his face. That made me a little sad...\nBut even so— I was really, really happy.": 109,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #16": 111,
          "We've been eating meat for so long now... but suddenly,\nI imagined where it might have come from, and I got chills.\nSo, I asked.\n\"Maruoris-sama, where does our meat... come from?\"": 112,
          "\"I'm sorry, Crediur... but please, try to understand.\nFrom another perspective, it's a rather convenient source of food.\"\n\nMaruoris-sama... I wanted you to deny it.": 113,
          "But... I've been eating it every day.\nAnd if there's nothing else, then I guess it can't be helped.\nSomehow, it made sense to me. Maybe I'm more broken than I realized.\nIt's scary how easy I accepted it.": 114,
          "Still, eating nothing but meat can't be good for my body.\nI really wish we had something else for a change.": 115,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #17": 117,
          "Maruoris-sama took me to the research facility.\nHe said he would show me the research process.\nHe was comparing the bodies of the people who had\nsucceeded and failed, lifting their skin to examine the difference.": 118,
          "Even though they were immortal, it seemed they were in great pain.\nThe person was screaming in agony, crying out for help,\nwhispering their family's names through sobs.\nIt became unbearable to be there, and I nearly cried as well.": 119,
          "Maruoris-sama calmly wrote something down and continued\ncomparing the bodies. It seemed he found something.\nIt seems black magic flows through the body to grant immortality,\nbut it continues to flow even in the bodies of those who failed.": 120,
          "Maruoris-sama made sure to tell me about it.\nI felt like I was becoming his assistant.\nI never want to see a scene like that again. Somewhere deep down,\nI can't believe that this research will save the world.": 121,
          "I couldn't help but ask: \"Maruoris-sama, why did you save me?\"\nDeep down, I couldn't trust Maruoris-sama,\nand fear began to slip from my mouth—\nthings I was scared to even think about.": 122,
          "I was about to ask,\n\"Did you save me just so you could use my body for your research?\"\nbut before I could say anything, he suddenly embraced me.\nHe held me tightly.": 123,
          "I was scared, but at the same time,\nI felt incredibly safe.\nI cried, still being held by him.\nMaruoris-sama just quietly held me, embracing me tightly.": 124,
          "Then, he told me... that he loved me.\n": 125,
          "I... love you too.\nMaruoris-sama.": 126,
          "You've given me so much love...\nThank you. Maruoris-sama.": 127,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #18": 128,
          "I'm not used to seeing the research,\nbut I feel like I'm starting to get used to it little by little.\nEven so, I still can't imagine doing research on my own.": 129,
          "However, if this immortality research becomes successful,\npeople won't have to be killed by those crimson monsters anymore.\nI want to support Maruoris-sama's research.": 130,
          "Even so, what Maruoris-sama is doing is exactly as he said,\nkidnapping people and killing them.\nIt's the same thing.": 131,
          "...I've been observing Maruoris-sama's research closely,\nand it seems that, by injecting the black magic into the body,\nand then sleeping for several days as if dead,\nimmortality is attained.": 132,
          "...But more than ninety percent remain asleep.\nAnd the majority of them end up with their hearts stopping.\nThe people who seemed abandoned near the research facility\nwere all those who remained sleeping.": 133,
          "Even if immortality is achieved, it seems they still feel pain.\nThat's why some of them end up mentally breaking down.\nIn the end, those people seem to die as well.": 134,
          "...It seems that Maruoris-sama is the only one\nwho has completely succeeded so far.": 135,
          "Maruoris-sama carries out his research calmly,\nbut when we talk, I feel like he's holding something back.": 136,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #19": 138,
          "I saw something unbelievable.\n": 139,
          "Earlier, I saw a person outside the window.\nI thought they might be being chased by a monster,\nbut their steps were unsteady, and they didn't seem panicked,\nyet they clearly looked strange.": 140,
          "This person had large holes where their eyes and mouth should be,\nand from those holes, something like Maruoris-sama's black magic\nwas leaking out, wandering aimlessly.": 141,
          "However, looking at their face and hairstyle,\nI immediately realized they were one of the test subjects\nwho had been sleeping at the research facility.": 142,
          "I had planned to read a book and not accompany the research today,\nbut it might have actually been for the best.\nI need to report this as soon as Maruoris-sama returns.": 143,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #20": 145,
          "I want to know more about Maruoris-sama.\nMaruoris-sama doesn't talk much about the past.\nIt's probably something he doesn't like to discuss,\nbut still, there are things that I can't help but wonder about.": 146,
          "I'm really curious about what Maruoris-sama was doing at my age.\nBecause now, he seems so mature, but surely,\nMaruoris-sama must have been mischievous in his younger years.": 147,
          "But Maruoris-sama still didn't answer.\nHe just told me that by the time he was my age,\nhe was already under the tutelage of his master.\nAnd he was learning magic from them.": 148,
          "I wonder why Maruoris-sama hates his master so much.\nIt seems like Maruoris-sama really doesn't want to talk about it,\nbut then that makes me even more curious about\nhow awful his master must have been.": 149,
          "I'm sorry to bring up something that hurt Maruoris-sama's heart,\nbut it's been bothering me so much, so I asked.\n\"Why do you dislike your master so much, Maruoris-sama?\"": 150,
          "Maruoris-sama, as expected, made a slightly sad face,\nbut he still calmly answered me.\n\"...What do you think of my research?\"": 151,
          "\"At first, it was very scary, but I think it's valuable research.\"\nThat was my answer. Then Maruoris-sama said,\n\"My master did such things for no reason, enjoyed them,\nlaughed at them, and lived for them.\"": 152,
          "Maruoris-sama looked unusually angry at that moment...\nAnd I think, at that time, I felt the same way as Maruoris-sama.\nTo do such things without any reason is unforgivable.": 153,
          "Also, even though Maruoris-sama seems so calm about it,\nthe way he referred to his research as 'such things'\nmade me feel that conducting this research\nmust still be painful for him, and I felt a little relieved.": 154,
          "Maruoris-sama is kind,\nboth strong-willed and powerful.": 155,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #21": 157,
          "I want to try training in martial arts,\nbut I have no idea how to go about it.": 158,
          "If I try punching or kicking something,\nI'd just end up damaging the house...\nand simply swinging my arms won't make me any stronger.": 159,
          "As I thought, the best option is to have Maruoris-sama train me.\nI really do want to become stronger.\nRather than just being a protected assistant,\nI want us to protect each other.": 160,
          "I'm looking forward to tomorrow.\nI'll head to bed early tonight.": 161,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #22": 163,
          "Calling it 'black magic' all the time feels a bit off,\nso I wondered if Maruoris-sama's magic has an actual name.": 164,
          "When I asked, Maruoris-sama said it's called 'Corruption'—\nan impurity to nature and life.\nBut 'Corruption' has such a negative ring to it.\nA magic that grants immortality being called 'Corruption'...": 165,
          "I suggested calling it 'Favor' instead.\nI've actually been thinking about it for a while—\nif immortality can be achieved with stability,\nthen it would truly be a blessing bestowed by Maruoris-sama.": 166,
          "But... I can understand why he calls it 'Corruption'.\nIt looks dark, and it is a little frightening.\nAnd if Maruoris-sama has always called it that,\nthen maybe there's a reason behind it.": 167,
          "I worried that I might have made him feel bad,\nbut Maruoris-sama simply said, \"Thank you\",\nand gently patted my head.": 168,
          "He probably doesn't think much of the name,\nbut... he still understood my feelings.\nIf Maruoris-sama's research is to truly become a 'blessing',\nthen I have to do my best too!": 169,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #23": 171,
          "The stuffed doll I've been secretly making is almost finished.\nI wanted to show my gratitude to Maruoris-sama,\nso I've been making it little by little,\ncareful not to let him find out.": 172,
          "I only made one once before, together with my mother.\nSo I'm trying to remember how I did it, stitching it together\nwith all my effort. I can't wait to see it finished.\nI wonder if Maruoris-sama will be happy with the surprise.": 173,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #24": 175,
          "I apologize for reading your diary without permission.\nAnd I apologize for writing in it without permission.": 176,
          "I had placed protective magic on this house, foreseeing this.\nBut I underestimated the power of the Crimson Wrath's monsters.\nBecause of that, I put you through this. I'm sorry.": 177,
          "I've caused you so much worry because of me.\nBecause I was too caught up in my worthless past,\nI never gave you the answers you sought. I'm sorry.": 178,
          "By chance, I found a stuffed doll near where you had collapsed.\nBringing it to the lab would only dirty it,\nso I'll place it somewhere clean.\nEvery time I look at it, I'll think of you.": 179,
          "When you wake up, I'll tell you everything you want to know.\n\nMartial arts, the magic I kept hidden— I'll teach you all of it.": 180,
          "I'll gather plenty of books so you never grow bored.\n\nI'll find all kinds of ingredients so you can enjoy your meals.": 181,
          "I had long forgotten what it meant to have a family.\n\nI thought I'd never feel that kind of warmth again.": 182,
          "You are my daughter. I love you.\n\nI'm sorry, Crediur. Truly, I love you.": 183,
          "So please...\n\nOpen your eyes.": 184,
          "Let me see you smile again.\n\nLet me see you happy again.": 185,
          "Please, don't die.\n\nI beg you.": 186,
          "Open your eyes.": 187,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #25": 189,
          "Having my diary read is a little embarrassing, but...\nif it means Maruoris-sama will tell me everything I want to know,\nthen maybe it wasn't such a bad thing after all.": 190,
          "Right now, thanks to Maruoris-sama's 'Favor',\nI have been given a second life.\nMy strength has grown, and I can now wield magic.\nAnd strangely enough, I no longer feel hunger at all.": 191,
          "I was a success— an immortal experiment that worked.\nMaruoris-sama has saved me not once, but twice.\nIf I had failed...\nI suppose I would have simply died back then, wouldn't I?": 192,
          "I'm so glad...\n\nWhen the monsters attacked me, when my body was torn to shreds...\nAll I could think about was how I didn't want to die.": 193,
          "Truly... I'm so glad...\n\nMaruoris-sama, from this moment on, I will live by your side,\nfor the rest of my life.": 194,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #26": 196,
          "It seems I'm no exception for my skin to turn purple.\nI... don't really like seeing myself like this.\nBut Maruoris-sama's skin is still so pristine,\nso I asked him about it. Apparently, he creates it with magic.": 197,
          "Maruoris-sama is a truly great sorcerer.\nAnd yet, the fact that he still cares about his appearance...\nit's kind of endearing. I never really thought of him as human,\nbut for the first time, he felt... strangely human to me.": 198,
          "...Is that rude of me to say?": 199,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #27": 201,
          "Maruoris-sama has started cooking for me,\nusing ingredients from who knows where.\nBut... I'm not human anymore, you know?\nI don't need to eat. And he knows that.": 202,
          "That said, it's not like I can't eat.\nI can still taste things, and his cooking... it's really good.\nBut having him stare at me the entire time I eat...\nit makes it a little hard to enjoy my meal.": 203,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #28": 205,
          "The reason Maruoris-sama came to my village...\nMaybe... it wasn't to save it after all.\nHe just happened to arrive just as the village was being attacked.\nMaybe... protecting it was just a coincidence.": 206,
          "I decided to ask him about it. But... it was quite foolish of me.\nI said, \"Did you originally come to my village to take someone?\"\nAnd when I did, he looked... heartbroken.": 207,
          "I wasn't thinking.\nI panicked and blurted out,\n\"I mean, it doesn't really matter either way!\"\nWhat a stupid thing to say.": 208,
          "Then he answered,\n\"I didn't know the village existed. I rushed in because of screams.\nBut... if I had known, I probably would have taken someone.\"": 209,
          "Even after hearing that...\nI didn't feel much of anything.\nI just said, \"I see.\"\nAnd that was the end of the conversation.": 210,
          "Maruoris-sama is always in this uncertain place.\nToo cruel to be kind, but too kind to be truly cruel.\nAnd yet, even though he tells himself it's all 'for research',\nhe can't fully embrace that mindset either.": 211,
          "...I love that about him.\nBut at the same time... I can't help but worry.\n\nOne day, will his heart just... break?": 212,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #29": 214,
          "Thanks to Maruoris-sama's 'favor', I've become incredibly strong.\nI was a little worried, so I asked Maruoris-sama to come with me,\nand we went monster hunting together. But to my surprise,\nI defeated them in an instant!": 215,
          "And even more surprising—\nMaruoris-sama said, \"You're fine even without me.\"\nHe truly believes in my strength now!!": 216,
          "I'm so proud of the power Maruoris-sama granted me.\nBut something started to bother me. If I use this power,\nwouldn't I be able to defeat all the monsters around the area?\nBut it can't be that easy, so I decided to ask him.": 217,
          "It turns out that Maruoris-sama can't destroy these monsters.\nEven if we wiped them all out, they would just resurrect again.\n\nThen he started to tell me the story of Sword of Dreams, Arkos.": 218,
          "I've heard of Lord Arkos before.\nHe was with his followers, often visited many villages,\npatrolling and defending us. I'd hear amazing stories from them.\nThey would also give me sweets, so I loved the sword followers.": 219,
          "According to what they said, Lord Arkos was incredibly strong\nand managed to defeat all the monsters by himself, but was\nultimately defeated by one particularly massive creature of wrath.\nMaruoris-sama told me that monster is still out there...": 220,
          "Maruoris-sama's story was one I had heard before.\nHowever, there was one point that was completely different\nfrom what everyone else had said.\nLord Arkos, it seems, took his own life.": 221,
          "According to what everyone said, Lord Arkos had been constantly\nfighting this powerful monster of wrath, defeating it over and over.\nHowever, each time he fell, the monster only grew stronger.\nLord Arkos somehow endured this.": 222,
          "Maruoris-sama had been watching that battle all along.\n\nThe moment Lord Arkos attempted suicide came as a complete surprise.\n": 223,
          "As Maruoris-sama rushed to him, he was stopped by Lord Arkos,\nwho told him to stay away.": 224,
          "After Lord Arkos' death, all the monsters of wrath that spread\nacross the world simultaneously had their power weakened,\nallowing humanity to avoid extinction.": 225,
          "After that, Maruoris-sama kept the existence of this monster,\nwhich he calls \\c[18]Dial\\c[0], a secret.\nHe told me that within the black magic he calls 'Corruption',\nthere was a key to breaking the essence of wrath.": 226,
          "Since destroying him was impossible, research became his priority.\nHowever, any monster other than \\c[18]Dial\\c[0] can be defeated.\n\"If you are willing, I want to ask for your help to save people.\"\nMaruoris-sama said, concluding his story.": 227,
          "I accepted gladly. Now, I have the strength to help.\nFrom now on, I will work hard to save lives.\nJust as Maruoris-sama helped me,\nI want to help the people of the world.": 228,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #30": 230,
          "I set off on a journey to search for people and towns.\nAs the sun began to set, and I was thinking of returning,\nI heard loud voices and the roar of a wild beast.": 231,
          "When I rushed over, I found a town,\nand it was being attacked by a monster of wrath.\nI suddenly remembered my own village.\nI felt like my legs were moving faster than usual.": 232,
          "The damage was minimal, and the townspeople thanked me.\nThey invited me to stay at the town for the night.\nThough I worried I might cause Maruoris-sama concern,\nI decided to accept their kind offer.": 233,
          "The people of the town treated me warmly.\nThe family who hosted me was very kind.\nBut when I woke up in the morning and found no one in the house,\nI became suspicious and decided to leave the house for a while.": 234,
          "I stepped outside to find the house surrounded by a lot of people.\n\"Is that monster trying to blend in and eat us from the inside?\"\nSomeone said that. I remember feeling dizzy at that moment.": 235,
          "My skin had turned purple again without me noticing.\nWhile I was sleeping, I had relaxed, and my magic had worn off.\nThe people of the house must have seen that and consulted someone,\nleading to this situation. That's how it must have happened.": 236,
          "The townspeople didn't attack me.\nI... could only shake my head to show that I was different.\nEven so, their wariness seemed to remain unchanged.": 237,
          "\"I'm sorry, but we'd like you to leave the town.\"\nThat's what they said.\nThey didn't seem to doubt me at all.\nBut their caution never wavered.": 238,
          "I think they were scared.\nPerhaps a monster with intelligence had disguised itself,\nand was planning something, sneaking into the town.\nI think they were holding onto that fear.": 239,
          "I obeyed without resistance and left the town.\nJust as I was about to leave, I turned back...\nand one of the women from the crowd ran out,\napologized and gave me some bread.": 240,
          "The townspeople weren't at fault. It's this era,\nwhere people must live in fear of vague threats, that is to blame.\nAnd the monsters of wrath, that created this era of fear...\nIt's the monster at the core of it all, \\c[18]Dial\\c[0], that is at fault.": 241,
          "Even knowing that, it was still so sad.\nI'm sure, someday, I'll be able to get along with the townspeople.\nBut will that day come before the people of this era are gone?": 242,
          "\n\nPlease, let me confess to something.": 243,
          "When I stayed in the town,\nI thought to myself that if I could just blend in,\nperhaps I could offer someone to Maruoris-sama.\nI didn't doubt that for a second.": 244,
          "The townspeople were right to be cautious of me.\nIf I hadn't been treated that way,\nI might have truly tried to offer someone to Maruoris-sama.": 245,
          "\n\nI deeply regret the thought I had of threatening someone's life,\nand I am truly sorry.": 246,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #31": 248,
          "Suddenly, a sharp pain ran through my leg.\nWhen I looked at my foot, it had become all rotten.\nI'm immortal, so something like this shouldn't bother me,\nbut that wasn't the case.": 249,
          "It was unbearably painful, and it continued to spread,\nslowly corroding my body from my foot,\nto my waist, and then to my chest.": 250,
          "The horror of \\c[29]Plague\\c[0] had been previously taught to me, both\nby the villagers and by Maruoris-sama.\nI was told over and over again to stay away from the red forests\nand the trees with green trunks.": 251,
          "But now that I was immortal and no longer capable of dying,\nI thought I could help those suffering in the area,\nso I bravely ventured into the forest,\nonly to fall victim to the Plague.": 252,
          "The pain was maddening, but it was the perfect opportunity\nto truly confirm if I was immortal.\nIf I truly weren't, I would have died right there.\nWhile I was being consumed, my mind was filled with fear.": 253,
          "I remembered the test subjects from Maruoris-sama's research,\nwhose minds had been shattered. Once the mind breaks, it's over.\nI decided to focus all my awareness on keeping my mind strong,\ndoing everything in my power to avoid letting it break.": 254,
          "Even so, the corrosion reached my face,\nand feeling my left eye droop and melt away was agonizing.\nMy vision seemed to stretch upwards, expand sideways, and cave in,\nas if my body entire body was being turned into a distorted mess.": 255,
          "In that state, everything felt nothing but painful,\nand I repeatedly let out screams that I could barely manage.\nAt one point, my consciousness faded, and when it came back,\nmy body had returned to normal.": 256,
          "The terror of immortality, and the marvel of immortality.\nI felt both of these at once.\nEverything returned to the way it was.\nEverything, down to my nails, was perfectly restored.": 257,
          "I rushed to the lab, and Maruoris-sama comforted me.\nWhen I revived, there was no pain,\nbut my mind felt a bit wobbly, and my body was trembling.\nThanks to Maruoris-sama's comfort, I was able to calm down.": 258,
          "Then, Maruoris-sama told me that the next time I was afflicted,\nI should cut away the affected part of my body without hesitation.\nBut the pain will still be there, and it's terrifying.\nWhen I said this, Maruoris-sama seemed troubled.": 259,
          "I asked if there was any medicine or magic to detoxify it.\nMaruoris-sama told me there was no such magic.\nThe available medicine could only suppress the poison's rise.\nUltimately, I will still have to cut away the affected parts.": 260,
          "The repeated warnings to stay away from the Plague,\nI finally understood their meaning at that moment.\nBut what exactly is this Plague? Such an abnormal thing...\nI'll ask Maruoris-sama about it tomorrow.": 261,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #32": 263,
          "I asked Maruoris-sama about the Plague.\nMaruoris-sama said he didn't know.\nBut I could tell immediately it was a lie.\nHis voice was trembling.": 264,
          "I brought up the diary,\nusing what Maruoris-sama had written in it as leverage,\nand I asked him to tell me the truth.\nLooking back now, I realize how awful it was.": 265,
          "Maruoris-sama said he couldn't answer.\nIt didn't seem like he was hiding anything.": 266,
          "Would answering me lead to some kind of bad outcome?\nWhen I asked, he nodded.\nThat means answering would cause someone to punish us for it,\nas they have been watching us all along.": 267,
          "So, I continued to ask.\nThen Maruoris-sama nodded.\nIs this threat worse than the monsters of wrath?\nMaruoris-sama nodded.": 268,
          "Maruoris-sama was serious.\nAnd he truly looked terrified.\nThis was the first time I had seen Maruoris-sama so afraid.": 269,
          "But Maruoris-sama still spoke.\nHe said the Plague was our fault.\nHe wouldn't say anything more.\nHis face was hidden behind his mask.": 270,
          "It felt as if the world had closed off into darkness.\nIs that threat watching me now as well?\nAn uncertain threat. Terrifying.": 271,
          "I have to ask Maruoris-sama.\nI can't sleep peacefully until I do.": 272,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #33": 274,
          "I poured out all my anxieties.\nMaruoris-sama apologized for causing me to feel anxious,\nand he took me to a cave near the laboratory.": 275,
          "It was a place I was always warned not to enter,\nno matter how curious I got. But this time, I was allowed in.\nWith Maruoris-sama by my side, I felt a sense of security,\nand I was almost lightheaded with excitement.": 276,
          "Inside, it was filled with sparkling crystals, a mystical scene.\nHowever, a chill I felt suddenly made me forget about everything.\nIt felt like something cold was invading the very core of my body.\nI can still clearly remember that feeling.": 277,
          "In the center of the cave, I felt it one more time,\nand Maruoris-sama showed the inside of it to me.\nInside, there was... ~ √": 278,
          "Something reached out for my body.\nThat something embraced my head, and it began to invade my mind.\nWhen I think of that thing,\nit keeps invading deeper and deeper into my mind.": 279,
          "But when I stop thinking about it, it all disappears.\nHowever, that doesn't mean I can forget.": 280,
          "When Maruoris-sama speaks with me,\nI wonder if he has ever been overcome by this sensation.\nI regret knowing what I now know.\nBut if I didn't know, it wouldn't matter.": 281,
          "However, if it were something ignorance could resolve,\nMaruoris-sama would have explained it to me that way.\nThe fact that I mustn't remember it is troublesome, but if it were\nthat easy I feel like Maruoris-sama would have hinted at it.": 282,
          "That thing is certainly a huge threat,\nand it seems safe to assume that everything Maruoris-sama\ncannot speak of is related to it.": 283,
          "Considering that, it seems Maruoris-sama has taught me everything\nabout the Crimson Wrath monsters without holding anything back.\nIt seems I can safely conclude that it's unrelated to the\nCrimson Wrath.": 284,
          "But I can't definitively decide.\nAfter all, I don't know why such monsters were born.\n\nTomorrow, I'll ask Maruoris-sama about it.": 285,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #34": 287,
          "He doesn't know.\nThat was Maruoris-sama's answer.\nAnd he said that the research aims to\nuncover that very thing.": 288,
          "If Maruoris-sama doesn't know,\nthen the possibility cannot be ruled out.": 289,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #35": 291,
          "Today, I was really surprised.\nI never expected Maruoris-sama to come crying to me.\nI was truly shocked.": 292,
          "Until now, he must have been holding in so much pain.\nBeing the one Maruoris-sama can rely on,\nI... Crediur, am so happy.": 293,
          "Ah... Maruoris-sama.\nI feel like I might be starting to feel something I shouldn't.": 294,
          "\\c[30]Diary Entry #36": 296,
          "Today, a strange test subject was born.\nSuddenly, it ran straight outside the research facility.": 297,
          "Those who are bestowed with favor usually wake up slowly.\nAnd they all inevitably check their surroundings.\n\nHowever, that test subject was absolutely in a rush.": 298,
          "Maruoris-sama captured it with magic, but\nimmediately, abnormalities were observed.\nIt started screaming, \"Don't look! don't look!\".": 299,
          "It was wildly moving its eyes,\nmaybe not so much because it was aware of us watching,\nbut more in a seemingly maddened state,\nas if it couldn't see us at all.": 300,
          "It kept getting violent, we had to use Maruoris-sama's\nmagic to gag and hold them down.\nMaruoris-sama seems to want to include this in the research too.": 301,
          "Its skin wasn't very purple,\nso it seems unlikely that immortality has been attained.\nHowever, its frantic behavior was concerning,\nand the words \"don't look\" are quite puzzling.": 302,
          "I wonder if it has something to do with that existence.": 303
        },
